      "message": "Would it make sense to use the Gerrit API version as the Bazel module version here, as is done in Gerrit core?\n\n```python\n\nGERRIT_API_VERSION \u003d \"3.12.0\"\nmodule(\n    name \u003d \"com_googlesource_gerrit_bazlets\",\n    version \u003d GERRIT_API_VERSION\n)\n```\n\nAlternatively, we could define:\n\n```python\nBAZLETS_VERSION \u003d GERRIT_API_VERSION\n```\n\nand use it in both places:\n\n```python\nBAZLETS_VERSION \u003d \"3.12.0\"\nmodule(\n    name \u003d \"com_googlesource_gerrit_bazlets\",\n    version \u003d BAZLETS_VERSION\n)\n[...]\ngerrit_api_version(\n    name \u003d \"gerrit_api_version\",\n    version \u003d BAZLETS_VERSION,\n    visibility \u003d [\"//visibility:public\"],\n)\n```\n\nThis would avoid duplicating the version string and keep the module and API versions in sync.",
